If nothing else will work, you can do what I did the time I threw my
quest artifact into the water of the medusa level -- use a ring of poly
control and a ring of polymorph to change into a creature that can
survive underwater (such as a xorn), then simply walk into the water
(having carefully either removed anything that might be damaged by
water or placed it in a handy oilskin sack first),  pick it up, and
come back out.

Come to think of it, I bet that if you get inside the castle and poly
into a xorn, you could
phase into the wall holding the Bell of Opening, pick it up, and walk
back out. Xorns can travel underwater AND can walk through walls.

Word of caution: If  you choose to do this,  make sure you take off
your armor and cloak first, or you'll burst them.  Xorns are larger
than human.

Also, don't take too long .. without an amulet of unchanging, you'll
revert to your normal form. It's embarrassing to have that happen
underwater.   I don't even want to imagine what happens if you revert
while in a wall.  

